WEBVTT

NOTE A story with a fictional family. Every paper shown is an invented sample.

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.330
All of Aama’s medical history lives in a plastic bag under the bed.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.360
Her new doctor asks for last year’s thyroid report.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.170
It isn’t in the bag.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.560
There is another way.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.480
At the hospital gate, Sita photographs Aama’s report.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.300
The photo is kept exactly as it is. That is the record.

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.810
Two readers read it separately. Only what both agree on is shown.

8
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.210
A smudged value isn’t guessed. It’s left empty.

9
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.760
In Kathmandu, Bikash checks every value against the photo of the paper.

10
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.440
In Pokhara, Aama shows a QR code, not a bag.

11
00:00:53.800 --> 00:01:00.440
The doctor reads exactly what the paper says, and can see the original.

12
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.990
That evening, Bikash stops the share. After that, the link shows nothing.

13
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.710
The paper stays. The history moves.

14
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.840
Abhilekh. Your medical history, with you.
